# Spec 019 AC-5/AC-6/AC-7, automatic (spec 013): the playground's ray moved with the stick (first-hit lines), the
# water bit of the mask toggled (the ray passes the pool), the three modes (screenshots), one-way cells ignored,
# touches on the bottom screen (what is under each point), then the self-check, whose checksum lines must be the
# PC's bit for bit, then the bench (rays < 2 ms per frame, points <= 0.1 us per box, moves recorded).
# PC:      nnh run queries --pc --script examples/queries/tests/check.nnhs
# Console: nnh run queries --script examples/queries/tests/check.nnhs   (Homebrew Launcher open, press Y)
#
# The expected lines below are the PC's (pc-debug). The first-hit and "under:" lines change only if the room, the
# moves below or the queries change; the checksum lines only if the script in self_check.cpp or the collision module's
# arithmetic changes: then run `QUERIES_DEMO=check NNH_EXIT_AFTER_FRAMES=90 build/pc-debug/examples/queries/queries.exe`,
# copy its lines here and kQueriesCheckGolden into self_check.hpp (and the checkpoints into
# tests/queries_example/test_self_check.cpp).
fail-on "] E "
fail-on "queries: FAIL"
# A bench target missed fails the run too, but only at the bench's verdict line ("queries bench: FAIL (rays)"),
# logged after every bench number, so one run reports the rays, their split, the points and the moves.
fail-on "queries bench: FAIL"

# First hit: the target starts at (330, 200); the ray stops flush on a wall's left face.
wait 30
screenshot first
# The stick moves the target 2 px per frame: left 90 frames, then down 8.
stick circle -1 0
wait 90
stick circle 0 0
wait 5
stick circle 0 -1
wait 8
stick circle 0 0
wait 10
expect "queries: first hit cell 6,9 solid fraction 0.5909 normal 0,-1" 1
screenshot pool

# Without the water bit the ray goes over the pool ("queries: mask 0x1D" comes in the same frame, just before).
tap A
expect "queries: first hit none" 10
wait 10
screenshot water
tap A
expect "queries: first hit cell 6,9 solid fraction 0.5909 normal 0,-1" 10
wait 10

# The modes (X): all hits with the cells crossed, then a box cast, then back.
tap X
expect "queries: mode all" 10
wait 10
screenshot all
tap X
expect "queries: mode cast" 10
wait 10
screenshot cast
tap X
expect "queries: mode first" 10
wait 10
tap Y
expect "queries: one-way ignored" 10
wait 10
tap Y
expect "queries: one-way blocks" 10
wait 10

# What is under a touch: the bottom screen shows the room from world x 40.
touch 72 152
expect "under: cell 7,9 solid layers 0x2 tile 2 boxes 0" 5
wait 5
untouch
wait 10
touch 132 124
expect "under: cell 10,7 empty layers 0x0 tile 4 boxes 1" 5
wait 5
untouch
wait 10
touch 210 82
expect "under: cell 15,5 one-way layers 0x1 tile 3 boxes 0" 5
wait 5
screenshot touch
untouch
wait 10

# The self-check (SELECT): 4096 rays and 512 box casts, a checksum every 1024 rays, then the verdict.
tap SELECT
expect "queries: self-check started" 20
expect "queries: 1024 sum 36C6AD9D" 60
expect "queries: 2048 sum 6A48E776" 60
expect "queries: 3072 sum F9B05D2F" 60
expect "queries: 4096 sum C8724E5B" 60
expect "queries: PASS 4ACAA177" 60
wait 10
screenshot self-check

# The bench (SELECT): about 20 s; each line PASS or FAIL against its target, the split and the move times recorded,
# then the verdict ("queries bench: PASS", or FAIL and the run fails). The split ("queries bench: rays split ...")
# comes in the frame of the rays line and the verdict in the frame of the move line: an expect matches from the
# frame after the previous one, so those two lines are in the log but not expected on their own.
tap SELECT
expect "queries bench: started" 20
expect "queries bench: rays avg" 700
expect "queries bench: points avg" 400
expect "queries bench: PASS" 400
wait 10
screenshot bench
end
